{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-dq-squared","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:dq-squared","kind":"proposition","title":"$d_q^2$ does not vanish","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-categorical-q-ext-deriv"],"proofs":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-dq-squared"],"tags":["q-deformation","exterior-derivative"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.dq_squared","text":"dq-squared.md","leanSource":"dq-squared.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:dq-squared\"></a><p>The archimedean specialisation yields <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">d_q^2\\alpha =  q^{-1}(1 - q^{-1})d\\varTheta \\wedge \\mathcal{L}_\\xi\\alpha</code>. Here <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">d\\varTheta</code> operates as the symplectic form on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H</code>. <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">d_q^2 = 0</code> if and only if <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q = 1</code> or <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\alpha</code> is Reeb-invariant.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/dq-squared.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"4.27.1","page":"b/prop-dq-squared","qa":{"counts":{"pass":90,"fail":1,"warn":0,"na":13,"unknown":0,"stale":80},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":1}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.Core.dq_squared","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/dq-squared.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
